export const body = /* #__PURE__ */ JSON.parse("[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"A finance process associate supports a defined financial workflow by checking information, processing authorised tasks, monitoring a queue, investigating exceptions, updating records, and escalating items that need another person's decision. The title is broad: one employer may use it for accounts payable or reporting, another for banking, payments, lending, reconciliation, client operations, or securities support. The actual process and authority in the job description matter more than the title.\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"This guide focuses on finance and BFSI work rather than generic business-process outsourcing. It explains transferable responsibilities and safe practice examples without claiming that every associate performs every task, uses the same system, or qualifies through one course.\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"What does a finance process associate do?\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"The associate usually owns one or more steps inside a larger operating process. Work arrives through a system, file, request, case, or scheduled control. The associate checks whether the item belongs in the queue, whether required information is present, and whether the evidence supports the next permitted action. Straight-through items can follow the documented process; incomplete, unusual, late, or conflicting items become exceptions that need investigation or escalation.\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"items\":[\"Receive and organise cases, transactions, documents, reports, or requests for the correct process and period.\",\"Validate identifiers, dates, amounts, status, account information, approvals, and required supporting evidence.\",\"Perform permitted processing steps and record the result in the authorised system or control file.\",\"Compare expected and actual records, identify breaks or missing information, and maintain an exception queue.\",\"Write a clear case note showing the issue, evidence checked, current owner, deadline, and next action.\",\"Escalate items outside authority, tolerance, service level, or documented procedure instead of improvising a correction.\",\"Support reporting, reconciliations, quality checks, and hand-offs to upstream or downstream teams.\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Common finance-process work areas\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Accounting and reporting support\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"An accounting process can involve invoice or expense checks, journal support, ledger review, account reconciliation, period-close schedules, and reporting evidence. The associate may prepare or validate information but should not assume authority to approve an entry, accounting treatment, or final report. Real work follows the entity's chart of accounts, policies, review requirements, and applicable standards.\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"Review accounting basics for finance operations\",\"href\":\"/resources/accounting-basics/\",\"routeId\":\"resource-accounting-basics\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Banking and loan operations\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Banking work can include onboarding checks, service requests, document intake, loan-processing support, repayment or status updates, and controlled communication. The associate follows the process and records evidence; credit approval, exceptions, customer commitments, and account changes require the authority defined by the institution. Product terms and customer data must stay within authorised systems and channels.\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Payments and reconciliation\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"A payments or reconciliation queue may contain unmatched, failed, duplicate, late, or incomplete records. The associate confirms the scope and matching rule, compares the available source records, classifies the break, records the evidence, and routes the item to the responsible owner. The goal is not to force two files to agree; it is to explain the difference and verify the authorised resolution.\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"Learn the reconciliation workflow in finance\",\"href\":\"/resources/reconciliation-in-finance/\",\"routeId\":\"resource-reconciliation-in-finance\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Investment and securities operations\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"In securities or investment operations, an associate may support trade capture checks, confirmations, settlement status, cash or position reconciliations, corporate actions, fund records, or client reporting. These are operations and control activities, not permission to trade, advise, value every product, or alter a source record. Product knowledge and deadline awareness become important because an unresolved exception can affect later stages of the lifecycle.\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"See investment banking operations roles and workflows\",\"href\":\"/career-guides/investment-banking-operations/\",\"routeId\":\"career-guide-investment-banking-operations\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"A realistic daily operating rhythm\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":true,\"items\":[\"Start-of-day check: confirm expected files, queue status, previous open items, deadlines, and any approved handover notes.\",\"Prioritisation: separate routine items from material, aged, deadline-sensitive, customer-impacting, or control-sensitive exceptions.\",\"Processing: complete permitted tasks using the current procedure, required evidence, and correct system access.\",\"Investigation: compare source records and event history, record the first difference, and avoid assumptions about the cause.\",\"Communication: send concise updates that identify the case, impact, checks completed, owner, and next action.\",\"Review and closure: obtain required approvals, verify the resulting record, and preserve the audit or control trail.\",\"End-of-day handover: report open items, ageing, deadlines, dependencies, and clear ownership for the next shift or team.\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Not every team works by daily cut-offs or shifts, but the sequence shows the discipline behind operations: know the inventory, process the authorised work, make exceptions visible, and leave enough evidence for another person to continue safely.\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Fictional case: an unmatched payment\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"A fictional queue shows a customer payment of INR 25,000 in an internal file but no corresponding credit in the comparison report. The associate first confirms the account, currency, amount, transaction reference, value date, and reporting cut-off. The payment gateway status shows accepted, but the settlement file for the period is incomplete. The associate records the source checked, labels the item unresolved rather than failed, assigns it to the approved payments owner, notes the next file time, and keeps the case open.\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"When the later file arrives, the payment appears with a next-day value date. The associate verifies the match under the documented rule, updates the case with the evidence, and closes it through the required review. The example demonstrates timing, evidence, and ownership. It does not describe a real customer or a universal payment procedure.\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Skills employers may test\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"items\":[\"Accuracy with structured information, documents, numbers, dates, references, and status codes.\",\"Spreadsheet basics such as sorting, filtering, lookups, conditional checks, pivot summaries, and protected source data.\",\"Process thinking: identify the input, check, decision owner, output, control, and downstream dependency.\",\"Exception writing that separates known facts, evidence, assumptions, and the next required action.\",\"Time management around queue ageing, service levels, cut-offs, reporting dates, and handovers.\",\"Professional communication with customers or internal teams without disclosing information or promising an unauthorised outcome.\",\"Judgement to stop, ask, and escalate when information conflicts or authority is unclear.\"]},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"How finance operations teams measure work\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Teams may measure volume, accuracy, turnaround time, service-level performance, ageing, rework, exception rates, customer impact, or control completion. The definition behind the number matters. A high completion count is not useful if records are wrong, material exceptions remain hidden, or cases are closed without evidence. A candidate should ask what quality means for that process and how a closure is verified.\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Finance process associate interview questions\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"items\":[\"How would you prioritise ten routine items and two exceptions near a deadline?\",\"What would you do if two approved reports show different amounts for the same reference?\",\"How do you check a spreadsheet before sending it for review?\",\"Describe a time you found an error, documented it, and communicated the next step.\",\"What information belongs in an exception or handover note?\",\"How would you respond if someone asked you to bypass a control to complete the queue faster?\",\"How do you protect confidential customer, account, or transaction data?\"]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"A strong answer explains the expected process, the evidence to check, the risk or deadline, the limits of the candidate's authority, and how the result would be verified. Freshers can use coursework, volunteering, projects, or fictional case exercises; they should not claim access to systems or customer data they have never handled.\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"Practise finance operations interview questions\",\"href\":\"/resources/investment-banking-interview-questions/\",\"routeId\":\"resource-investment-banking-interview-questions\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"A safe portfolio project for freshers\"},{\"type\":\"list\",\"ordered\":true,\"items\":[\"Create twenty fictional transactions with unique IDs, dates, amounts, accounts, and statuses.\",\"Create a second fictional report containing timing differences, one duplicate, one missing item, and one amount variance.\",\"Write the matching rule before using formulas so the logic can be reviewed.\",\"Build an exception log with classification, evidence, owner, ageing, priority, and next action.\",\"Prepare a one-page summary showing the control total, matched items, open breaks, and what still requires approval.\",\"Explain how you protected the source sheets and why you did not overwrite a record to force a match.\"]},{\"type\":\"callout\",\"title\":\"Use only invented or authorised data\",\"text\":\"A portfolio should demonstrate reasoning, formulas, documentation, and control awareness. Never publish employer, client, customer, account, transaction, or system data.\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Career progression and adjacent roles\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Experience in a process role can support movement toward senior processing, reconciliation, quality, reporting, controls, payments, loan operations, settlements, client operations, or team coordination. Progression is not automatic and titles vary. Evidence of reliable work, stronger exception handling, root-cause analysis, process improvement, product learning, and stakeholder communication is more useful than assuming that a generic associate title leads to one fixed path.\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"Read the Finance Operations career guide\",\"href\":\"/career-guides/finance-operations/\",\"routeId\":\"career-guide-finance-operations\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":2,\"text\":\"How this topic relates to Centaur Careers\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Finance Operations is one of the modules inside Centaur Careers' Financial Operations Masterclass. Accounting, reporting, loan processing, credit analysis, risk context, and reconciliation can help learners understand process-associate job descriptions. This article does not create a separate process-associate class or promise a title, employer, salary, city, or vacancy. Review the current curriculum and written program terms before enrolling.\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"Explore the Finance Operations module\",\"href\":\"/courses/finance-operations/\",\"routeId\":\"finance-operations\"},{\"type\":\"link\",\"label\":\"Review the Financial Operations Masterclass\",\"href\":\"/courses/\",\"routeId\":\"courses\"},{\"type\":\"faq\",\"question\":\"Is a finance process associate an accounting role?\",\"answer\":\"It can support accounting, but the title can also cover banking, payments, lending, reconciliation, securities, reporting, or customer operations. Read the process, outputs, systems, and authority in the actual job description.\"},{\"type\":\"faq\",\"question\":\"Can a fresher apply for finance process associate roles?\",\"answer\":\"Some employers recruit graduates for entry-level process roles, while others require specific education, experience, shifts, tools, or product knowledge. Demonstrate accuracy, spreadsheet skills, process reasoning, communication, and safe handling of information, then compare each vacancy with your profile.\"},{\"type\":\"faq\",\"question\":\"What is the most important skill for a process associate?\",\"answer\":\"Accuracy is foundational, but the role also needs prioritisation, evidence-based exception handling, clear communication, and the judgement to escalate instead of acting beyond authority.\"},{\"type\":\"faq\",\"question\":\"Does Centaur Careers offer a separate process associate course?\",\"answer\":\"No separate process-associate class is claimed here. Relevant workflow skills are discussed within the broader Financial Operations Masterclass and its Finance Operations learning area.\"}]");
